            <ArticleTitle>Penetrating ulcer of ascending thoracic aorta in syphilis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>16-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Penetrating aortic ulcers (PAUs) are rare exotic pathological entities, classically located in the descending thoracic aorta. Their association with syphilis has never been reported. We describe a first case of a patient with cardiovascular syphilis presenting as PAU in the ascending aorta.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright 2004 Wiley-Liss, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
